{
  "format": "selin-gate-conformance",
  "version": 1,
  "generator": "cargo run -q --locked -p archon_kernel --example selin_gate_vectors",
  "consumers": ["archon_kernel/tests/gate_conformance.rs", "test/gate_vectors.test.mjs"],
  "contract": [
    "V and J must each be a finite number in [0, 1]. Anything else (NaN, Infinity, -Infinity, or a value outside [0, 1]) is refused by the domain check: signal abort, passed false, rejection_reason exactly domain_refusal, chi and mirror_chi NaN. Nothing is clamped into range, and no invariant is computed from a refused score. -0 is zero, so it is inside the domain.",
    "Otherwise chi = sqrt((V^2 + (1 - J)^2) / 2), mirror_chi = chi(1 - V, J), and four more checks run:",
    "floor: chi < threshold aborts (threshold null means the default, 1/sqrt2).",
    "mirror: chi - mirror_chi < 0.15 aborts.",
    "components: V < 1/sqrt2 or 1 - J < 1/sqrt2 aborts.",
    "ceiling: chi > sovereign_ceiling suspends (held for escalation, not released).",
    "signal is abort if any check aborted, else suspend if the ceiling held, else execute. passed is signal == execute, and rejection_reason is null exactly when passed.",
    "refused_by lists every check that refused, in the order above.",
    "The constants are the doubles given below. sovereign_ceiling is the double nearest the literal 0.9539392014169456 (its shortest form is 0.9539392014169455). sqrt(0.91) evaluated in doubles is one float above it, so a consumer uses the literal and does not recompute it."
  ],
  "encoding": "Every number is a string: the shortest decimal that reads back as the same double, or NaN, Infinity, -Infinity. Rust's str::parse::<f64> and JS Number() then read identical bits. signal, passed and refused_by must match exactly; chi and mirror_chi within 1e-12, and NaN must be NaN. refused_by is read from rejection_reason: split it on ' | ', take the text of each part before its first ':', and look that tag up in tags.",
  "constants": {"chiral_floor": "0.7071067811865476", "sovereign_ceiling": "0.9539392014169455", "mirror_gap_min": "0.15"},
  "domain_refusal": "domain: V and J must each be a finite number in [0, 1]",
  "tags": {"domain": "domain", "Chiral Violation": "floor", "mirror": "mirror", "components": "components", "ceiling": "ceiling"},
  "rows": [
